    "result_text": "The full build is green. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `membershipNumber` field formatted `<customerCode>-M<YY>` (e.g. `SMI-0007-M26`), where `YY` is the last two digits of the registration date's year.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a derived getter `getMembershipNumber()`. It composes the existing `customerCode` and `registrationDate` fields via `String.format(\"%s-M%02d\", customerCode, registrationDate.getYear() % 100)`, returning `null` when either source is absent. Since the entity uses field-based JPA access, this read-only getter is not persisted; MapStruct auto-maps it onto the DTO by matching property name.\n\n2. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `membershipNumber` string property to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes the field in the REST response.\n\nDeriving the value from the owner's own fields (rather than storing it) keeps it seed-independent, which matches how the acceptance test checks it.\n\n**Tests:** `AcceptanceTest.coreMembershipNumberFormat` passes and the full `mvn test` run reports `BUILD SUCCESS` (1 test, 0 failures, 0 errors).",
